From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shiny <owner@shinychang.net>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:27:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Ghostty-style split view with seamless panes

- Cmd+D splits right and Shift+Cmd+D splits down (they no longer bookmark);
  Split Left and Split Up are in the File menu and the command palette.
  Chromium splits hold two tabs, so splitting a split only re-orients it.
- Cmd+Opt+arrows select the pane in that direction and fall back to the
  previous or next tab, or focus pane, when there is none. Keyboard focus
  moves with the pane, since BrowserView restores focus only outside a split.
- Cmd+Ctrl+arrows move the divider, Cmd+Ctrl+= evens it, Cmd+W closes the
  active pane; Swap Panes and Exit Split View are palette commands.
- In a split, Go to Anything opens tabs, URLs and history in the active
  pane; the tab it replaces stays open unless it is the split new-tab page.
- Panes are drawn edge to edge like a single tab: no inset, padding,
  outline, mini toolbar or divider gap. Web contents cover anything drawn
  over them, so the divider is resized from the keyboard only.
- smoke.mjs: 8 split checks, 30 in total.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
